<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>IAM and IAAAAA Explanation</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f6f9;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        h2 {
            color: #34495e;
            margin-top: 25px;
        }
        .box {
            background: white;
            padding: 15px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 6px solid #3498db;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        ul {
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        code {
            background: #eee;
            padding: 8px;
            display: block;
            margin-top: 10px;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>What is IAM?</h1>

    <div class="box">
        <p><strong>IAM (Identity and Access Management)</strong> is a system that controls 
        who can access what resources in a system or cloud environment.</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Right User</li>
            <li>Right Access</li>
            <li>Right Time</li>
            <li>Right Reason</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Used in cloud platforms like:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</li>
            <li>Microsoft Azure</li>
            <li>Google Cloud</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>IAAAAA Security Model</h2>

    <div class="box">
        <p><strong>IAAAAA stands for:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Identification</li>
            <li>Authentication</li>
            <li>Authorization</li>
            <li>Accounting</li>
            <li>Auditing</li>
            <li>Accountability</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>1. Identification</h3>
        <p>Who are you? (Username, Email, ID)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>2. Authentication</h3>
        <p>Prove it! (Password, OTP, Fingerprint)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>3. Authorization</h3>
        <p>What can you access? (Read, Write, Delete)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>4. Accounting</h3>
        <p>Tracks system usage and activity logs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>5. Auditing</h3>
        <p>Security team reviews logs for issues.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
        <h3>6. Accountability</h3>
        <p>Every action is traceable to a responsible user.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Flow Diagram</h2>

    <div class="box">
        <code>
User → Identify → Authenticate → Authorize → Log → Audit → Responsible
        </code>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
